    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Hohenzollern kingdom proclaimed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Königsberg</a> in 1701, built from scattered lands between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and the Baltic.</li><li>Its army and disciplined bureaucracy made a poor, small state a European great power under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-grand-duke-of-baden">Frederick II</a>.</li><li>Under Bismarck it defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and in 1871 united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> under its king.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Prussia’s first king was only ‘King in Prussia’, because part of Prussia still belonged to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>; Frederick II took the title ‘King of Prussia’ after the partition of 1772.</p></aside>
    </section>

